create.account user is not available on a stand-alone SD system, so %1\nwas not created.\n\nA stand-alone system installs no ssh server.  An account made this way is\ndenied the console and Remote Desktop, because it is meant to arrive over\nssh - so with no ssh server it could sign in nowhere at all.\n\nTo keep separate work separate, use a group account instead.  It needs no\nWindows user and no sign-in:\n\n    create.account group %1\n    logto %1\n\nTo make accounts for other people, install SD again and choose the full\ninstallation.
